meta {
  name: Upload File (Wrong User)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Error-path test: upload a file to a post owned by a different user.
  Expected: 403 { error: "Forbidden" }

  LIMITATION: The seed data only provides one test user (testuser).
  There is no seeded post owned by a different user to test against.
  This is a placeholder that hits GET /api/health so the collection
  run does not break.

  To truly test 403:
  1. Seed a second user and a post owned by that user
  2. Add an axios pre-request script (see upload-file.bru pattern)
  3. Use testuser's token to upload to the other user's post
  4. Assert _uploadStatus equals 403
}
